$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Compound 3b. In an oven-dried Schlenk flask, sodium
2-methyl-2-propanethiolate (3.12g, 2.1eq) was added to a solution of
1,2,4,5-tetrabromobenzene (5.00g, 12.3mmol) in DMF (35mL) and the
solution was stirred at 50°C for 5 hours. The contents of the vessel were
diluted with ether, treated with 20% KOH, and dried over anhydrous
magnesium sulfate. After concentration via rotary evaporation, the yellow
residue was sonicated with MeOH to obtain a colorless solid (3.78g, 74%).
1H NMR (400MHz, CDCl3) δ : 7.95 (s, 2H), 1.39 (s, 18H). 13C NMR (100MHz,
CDCl3) δ : 141.89, 136.73, 130.00, 49.43, 31.04. GC-MS: m/z: 412
(C14H20Br2S2 +), 300(100%). MP: 126°C.
