$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General methods for the preparation of
sulfones and sulfoxides: The sulfones and sulfoxides were synthesized
according to known literature procedures. 1-3 To a solution of the
corresponding phenol, thiophenol or thiophenolate and substituted
nitrobenzene, an equimolar amount of base for the thiophenol or 0.3
equivalents for the thiophenolate was added and heated to reflux. EtOH
and 0.1 M aqueous NaOH was used as the solvent and the base,
respectively, if not otherwise mentioned. After complete consumption of
the starting material the solvent was removed and a 1/1 mixture of water
and EtOAc was added. The aqueous phase was extracted twice with EtOAc.
The combined organic layers were dried over MgSO4 and the solvent was
removed in vacuum to yield the The crude sulfide. Method A) The sulfide
was dissolved in 5 ml acetic acid and an excess of 0.7 ml H2O2 was added
drop wise if not otherwise mentioned. After complete addition the
reaction mixture was heated to reflux. If necessary another equivalent of
H2O2 was added. After complete reaction the solvent was removed in
vacuum. 2,4-Dinitro-1-(phenylsulfonyl)benzene (3):
2,4-Dinitro-1-(phenylsulfonyl)benzene was synthesized according to Method
A) using 2,4-dinitrochlorobenzene (288 mg, 1.4 mmol) and sodium
thiophenolate (188 mg, 1.4 mmol). After column chromatographic
pruficiation (25 g SiO2, PE/EE : 3/1) and recrystallization from
EE/hexane,
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
