$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (Het)aryl Sulfides 3; General Procedure
Diiodobenzene 1 (0.2 mmol), (het)aryl thiol 2 (0.3 mmol), CuI (0.04
mmol), ligand L1 (0.04 mmol), and Cs2CO3 (0.4 mmol) were added to DMSO (1
mL) in a 25-mL round-bottomed flask equipped with a stirring bar. The
mixture was stirred at 100 °C for 18 h under N2 then cooled to r.t. H2O
(8 mL) was added and the resulting residue was extracted with EtOAc (3 ×
8 mL). The organic layers were combined, dried (MgSO4), and concentrated
under reduced pressure. The residue was purified by silica flash column
chromatography (petroleum ether). 2-Iodophenyl Phenyl Sulfide (3a)14
2-[(2-Iodophenyl)sulfanyl]aniline (3h) Brown solid; yield: 48 mg (74%).
mp 98-100 °C. IR (KBr): 3463, 1528, 1456, 1004, 732, 527 cm-1. 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 7.69 (d, J = 7.6 Hz, 1 H), 7.37 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 1
H), 7.22-7.17 (m, 1 H), 7.05 (t, J = 7.6 Hz, 1 H), 6.74-6.68 (m, 3 H),
6.52 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1 H), 3.83 (br s, 2 H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ
= 148.81, 141.46, 139.40, 137.69, 131.75, 128.65, 126.49, 125.85, 119.13,
115.66, 114.67, 95.76. HRMS (EI): m/z [M]+ calcd for C12H10INS: 326.9579;
found: 326.9579.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, Ullmann reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Copper-catalyzed selective single arylsulfanylation of aryl diiodides
with aryl thiols
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
