$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical procedure of the preparation of diaryl
sulfides: 1.5 mmol of phenyl polymeric styryliodonium salts (3a) and 1
mmol sodium p-methyl benzenethiolate were added to 10 mL of DMF. The
temperature was kept at 100°C for 10 h. Then the solution was poured into
100 mL cold water to precipitate the polymer. The aqueous layer was
extracted with ether (2 x 10 mL) and chloroform (15 mL). The combined
organic layer was washed with water (20 mL x 2) and dried over MgSO4.
After evaporated the solvent gave p-methylphenyl phenyl sulfide (5m). 5l:
purity 95%; yield 74%; oil (lit.10e oil). 1H-NMR (CCl4) δ: 6.56-7.56 (m,
9H), 3.70 (s, 3H); IR (film) ν (cm-1): 3020, 2920, 2820, 1585, 1490,
1070, 1030, 1000, 810, 755, 690.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM solid-supported reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of polymeric diaryliodonium salts and its use in preparation of
diaryl sulfides and diaryl ethers
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Huang, Xian; Zhu, Qing; Xu, Yongxi
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
