$DATUM 80-73-9
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4-(tert-butylthio)benzaldehyde (15). 4-fluoro-benzaldehyde (174mg, 1.85
mmol, 1.0 eq.) was dissolved in 15 ml DMI. NaStBu (312mg, 2.78 mmol, 1.5
eq.) was added and it was stirred for 20 hours at room temperature. The
reaction mixture was then extracted with water and TBME, the combined
organic phases were dried over Na2SO4, filtrated, evaporated and
chromatographed (silica gel, 3x12 cm, TBME:hexane 1:3) to give a
colorless liquid that tends to crystallize (266mg, 1.37 mmol, 74%). TLC:
Rf = 0.47 (TBME:hexane, 1:3). 1H-NMR (250 MHz, CDCl3, δ /ppm): 10.01 (1H,
s); 7.81 (2H, d, 3JHH = 8.59 Hz); 7.66 (2H, d, 3JHH = 8.08 Hz); 1.32 (9H,
s). 13C-NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3, δ /ppm): 192.1, 141.7, 137.4, 136.2, 129.8,
47.6, 31.5. MS (EI): 194.0 (18.5%, M+); 138.0 (94.9%); 109.0 (13.8%). EA:
calculated: C = 68.00, H = 7.26, found: C = 68.21, H = 7.41. IR(neat, G,
cm-1): 2962.5, 1701.1, 1593.1, 1164.9.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM New Cruciform Structures: Toward Coordination Induced Single Molecule
Switches
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
