$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for Synthesis of Compounds 2 A mixture of substituted
3-bromonitrobenzene (0.01 mol), cuprous thiophenolate (0.01 mol),
pyridine (1.5 mL), and quinoline (10 mL) was heated with stirring in an
oil bath at about 220°C for 2h. The hot solution was then poured into
cracked ice and excess conc. hydrochloric acid, standing for about 2h.
The mixture was extracted with ethyl ether, and the combined organic
layers were dried with anhyd. MgSO4, concentrated under reduced pressure
and purified by column chromatography on silica gel (petroleum ether) to
afford the pure product. 1-Nitro-3-phenylthiobenzene (2a). Yellow solid,
yield 73%. mp 43-44°C (lit.[24] 42.5°C); IR NMR (CDCl3) δ 7.99-8.04 (m,
2H), 7.39-7.51 (m, 7H). MS, m/e (%): 231 (M+, 100), 232 (M+ + 1, 18.76)
215 (5.12), 184 (76.61).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthetic study of substituted arylsulfonylphenylbenzamides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
