$DATUM 2-Methoxy-6-(3-methoxyphenyl)-1-[(4-methylphenyl)sulfanyl]naphthalene
(34b). A mixture of 1-bromo-2-methoxy-6-(3-methoxyphenyl)naphthalene 31a
(100 mg, 0.29 mmol, 1 eq) and sodium 4-methylbenzenethiolate (51 mg, 0.34
mmol, 1.2 eq) in dry DMF (10 ml) was refluxed for 11 h under nitrogen
atmosphere. The reaction mixture was poured in ice. The precipitate
formed was collected, washed with water and dried in a desiccator (73%
yield, 80 mg). The compound was pure enough to be used in the next step
without further purification. C25H22O2S; MW 386; 1H-NMR (acetone-d6): δ
8.13 (d, J = 1.9 Hz, 1H), 8.03 (d, J = 1.9 Hz, 1H), 7.91 (d, J = 8.8 Hz,
1H), 7.66 (dd, J = 1.9 Hz, J = 8.8 Hz, 1H), 7.50 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 1H),
7.45 (t, J = 8.2 Hz, 1H), 7.39 (t, J = 8.2 Hz, 1H), 7.33-7.29 (m, 3H),
7.03-6.96 (m, 4H), 3.88 (s, 3H), 3.85 (s, 3H), 2.78 (s, 3H).
