$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Ni(0)-Mediated Intramolecular C−S
Cross-coupling (General Procedure D) To a stirred slurry of Zn (130 mg, 2
mmol) and NiCl2 (65 mg, 0.5 mmol) in pyridine (0.5 mL) was added ethyl
crotonate (0.16 mL, 1.5 mmol) or bipyridine (94 mg, 0.6 mmol) at room
temperature. Then the temperature rose to 55 °C and vigorous stirring was
continued for 15 minutes. The resulting Ni(0) complex was cooled to room
temperature, to which the solution of substrate (1 mmol) in pyridine (1
mL) and MeOH (10 mL) was added dropwise over a 1~1.5 h period. Then the
reaction mixture was further stirred for 3.5 h and filtered with a short
plug of silica (elution with 80 mL Et2O). The filtrate was washed with
HCl (1N), water and brine, dried over MgSO4, filtered and concentrated.
The crude product was purified by flash chromatography on silica gel to
afford desired thioether. 3a was prepared according to General Procedure
D. 3e was prepared according to General Procedure D. Colorless oil (73%
yield). Rf = 0.43 (petroleum ether/EtOAc = 2 : 1); IR (film): νmax =
2951, 2919, 1723, 1597, 1436, 1405, 1345, 1291, 1243, 1187, 1159, 1113,
1032, 987, 957, 813, 764, 742, 685, 654, 582 cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3): δ = 8.06 (d, J = 1.6 Hz, 1H), 7.83 (dd, J = 8.0, 1.6 Hz, 1H),
7.64 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 7.54 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H), 7.25 (d, J = 8.0 Hz,
2H), 3.90 (s, 3H), 3.74 (brs, 2H), 2.71 (d, J = 3.6 Hz, 2H), 2.42 (s,
3H), 2.10 (quint, J = 5.2 Hz, 2H) ppm; 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ =
165.9, 143.5, 142.4, 142.3, 137.9, 133.1, 131.2, 130.0, 129.5 (2C),
128.7, 127.6 (2C), 52.3, 49.6, 31.1, 30.4, 21.6 ppm; HRMS (ESI): m/z
calcd for C18H19NO4S2Na+ [M+Na]+: 400.0648, found: 400.0663.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM slow addition of substrate solution stage 2, in-situ generated catalyst
(stage 1)
