$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Catalytic Procedure for the
S-Arylation of Thiols with Aryl Iodides. The catalyst (0.05 mmol) was
dissolved in dioxane (1 mL) in an ampule. The aryl iodide (1.2 mmol), the
thiol (1.0 mmol), and the base, LiOtBu (2 mmol), were added under a
nitrogen atmosphere. The reaction was stirred at 110 °C for 24 h in an
oil bath. The reaction mixture was allowed to cool to room temperature
and treated with ethyl acetate (15 mL) and water (5 mL). The organic and
aqueous layers were then separated, and the organic layer was evaporated
to dryness. The residue was purified by flash chromatography on silica
gel. 4-Methylphenyl phenyl sulphide13. Following the general method,
complex 2 (0.05 mmol), 4-iodotoluene (1.2 mmol), thiophenol (1.0 mmol),
and the base LiOtBu (2 mmol) were heated in dioxane (1 mL) at 110°C for
24 h. Chromatography: SiO2, petroleum ether. Yield: 72% as yellow oil. 1H
NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.43-7.20 (m, 9H), 2.49 (s, 3H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Ullmann reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
