$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General experimental procedures for the synthesis of Benzo[b]pyrido
[2,3-f] [1,4] thiazepin -11(10H)-ones. A 25 mL schlenk tube equipped with
a magnetic stiring bar was charged with halogenous benzenethiol (2a-2e)
or 3-chloro-5-(trifluoromethyl)pyridine-2-thiol (5) (0.5 mmol, 1.0
equiv), N-substituted nitrobenzamides (1a-1i) (0.6 mmol, 1.2 equiv), KOH
(84 mg, 1.5 mmol, 3.0 equiv) and then 15 mL of DMF or DMSO was added via
syringe at room temperature and the mixture was prestirred for about 15
minutes. Then the reaction was stirred at 150 °C. After the reaction was
completed, the mixture was diluted with brine (40 mL) and extracted with
ethyl acetate twice (2×30 mL). The combined organic layers were dried
over MgSO4 and the solvent was removed in vacuo to afford a residue. The
crude product was then purified by column chromatography on silica gel to
give the pure product.
6-Chloro-2-nitro-10-propyldibenzo[b,f][1,4]thiazepin-11(10H)-one (3a)
Yellow solid; yield 72%. mp 105-107 °C; 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.54
(d, J = 2.4 Hz, 1H), 8.14-8.11 (dd, J = 2.7, 8.7 Hz, 1H), 7.70 (d, J =
8.4 Hz, 1H), 7.35-7.26 (m, 3H), 4.74-4.64 (m, 1H), 3.59-3.41 (m, 1H),
1.74-1.62 (m, 2H), 0.96 (t, J = 7.5, 2.1 Hz, 3H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3)
δ 166.3, 148.2, 145.5, 144.8, 139.7, 137.6, 134.8, 132.6, 130.2, 127.9,
126.6, 125.0, 124.8, 53.1, 21.4, 11.5. HRMS (ESI): calcd for
C16H13ClN2O3S (M+ H)+ 349.0408, found 349.0406.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM combinatorial, green chemistry, regioselective, Smiles rearrangement
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM One Pot Regioselective Synthesis of a Small Library of
Dibenzo[b,f][1,4]thiazepin-11(10H)-ones via Smiles Rearrangement
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Zhao, Yongmei; Dai, Qiaoling; Chen, Zhi; Zhang, Qihui; Bai, Yongcheng;
Ma, Chen
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM ACS Combinatorial Science (2013), 15(2), 130-134

