$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of OCMe2CMe2OP(S)SC6H4NHC(O)Me A weighed amount of
p-bromoacetanilide (1.13 g) was treated with ammonium tetramethyl
ethylene dithiophosphate (1.21 g) in benzene (~45 ml). The reaction
mixture was refluxed for -28 hrs. The reaction is fast in the presence of
strong base (EtONa) and completes within -10 hrs of refluxing in benzene.
The NH4Br precipitated was filtered off and the excess of solvent was
removed under reduced pressure. The product obtained was light yellow
sticky solid. The above procedure was adopted for all the other
reactions. Relevant data are given in Table III. Yield 72%. The compound
on analysis show; C. 48.00; H. 5.72; S, 18.01 % Calcd. for
CMe2CMe2OP(S)SC6H5NHC(O)Me: C, 48.69; H, 5.80; S, 18.55%. 1H (δppm):
1.58, s, 12H(Me); 7.33, m, 4H(Ph); 2,9, s, 3H(COMe); 5.5, bs, 1H(NH); 31P
(δppm): 99.88
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Organic derivatives of alkylene dithiophosphates. Part II. Synthesis and
properties of 2-acetanilide (benzanilide) derivatives of alkylene
dithiophosphates
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Purwar, Ratana; Sharma, Mukesh K.; Sharma, Rajnish K.; Nagar, Padam N.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Phosphorus, Sulfur and Silicon and the Related Elements (2001), 17415-23

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME304 STEP1
$RXN



