$DATUM 68-12-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4-(Methylthio)acetophenone To a stirred suspension of sodium
thiomethoxide (2.5 g, 36 mmol) in DMF (100 mL) was added
4’-chloroacetophenone (4.63 mL, 36 mmol) dropwise over 30 min. After the
addition was complete, the solution was stirred at room temperature for a
further 30 minutes. The solvent was decanted off and the resulting yellow
solid was recrystallized (CH2Cl2/petrol). The product (4.3 g, 72%) as a
pale yellow powder. M.p. 71-72 °C (lit. m.p.2 71-73 °C); 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 7.86 (d, J = 8.5 Hz, 2H), 7.26 (d, J = 8.5 Hz, 2H), 2.57 (s,
3H), 2.52 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 197.2, 145.9, 138.5, 128.7,
125.0, 26.4, 14.8.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Aryl Methyl Sulfides as Substrates for Rhodium-Catalyzed Alkyne
Carbothiolation: Arene Functionalization with Activating Group Recycling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
