$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Preparation of OCMe2CMe2OP(S)SC6H4NHC(O)Me A
weighed amount of p-bromoacetanilide (1.13 g) was treated with ammonium
tetramethyl ethylene dithiophosphate (1.21 g) in benzene (~45 ml). The
reaction mixture was refluxed for -28 hrs. The reaction is fast in the
presence of strong base (EtONa) and completes within -10 hrs of refluxing
in benzene. The NH4Br precipitated was filtered off and the excess of
solvent was removed under reduced pressure. The product obtained was
light yellow sticky solid. The above procedure was adopted for all the
other reactions. Relevant data are given in Table III. Yield 72%. 1H
(δppm): 1.45, s, 3H(Me); 4.9, m, 1H(OCH); 4.0, m, 2H(OCH2); 7.4, m,
4H(Ph); 5.4, bs, 1H(NH); 3.0, s, 3H(Me); 31P (δppm): 87.19
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Organic derivatives of alkylene dithiophosphates. Part II. Synthesis and
properties of 2-acetanilide (benzanilide) derivatives of alkylene
dithiophosphates
